ok at the inventory in those channels, uh, I mean, there's just no- these from a, from a compressor perspective. Which is obviously the one that has, uh, the biggest size of the distribution that work. And, and it is also a more particularly towards the Gardner Denver branded products. Uh, you know, we don't tend to have a lot of inventory because these, these are particularly smaller distributors, more so <unk>, uh, more than localized. They don't tend to, to put a lot of cash upfront to have compressors on the shelf, so to speak. I mean, maybe on the smaller compressors, they, they may. Uh, but not on the medium to high level compressors. And, and the inventory will come in more on consumables, aftermarket I'm… really move fairly, uh, fa- fairly well. I mean, they turn pretty quickly. Vicente, just so I'm clear, is it a stabilization at a low level after the initial shock in ITS, or have you seen some, you know, little improvement in order sequentially. And I'll be curious, is that more short cycle or long cycle? Yeah, I know. Yeah. Great question. Yeah, it is… I would, I would categorize it as a set of civilization, and uh, uh, initially, and then obviously when you look within the month, I mean, a- at the month of April, you know, there some, uh, slight improvement on the second half of April c- But again, was that more short cycle improvement? Short cycle. Yeah. More short cycle. Yeah. Short cycle. All right. Thank you v- Thank you very much. Appreciate it. Sure. Your next question comes from Josh Poklinsky f-… is open. Hi, good morning all? Morning Josh. Um, so Vicente, I guess, you know, e- everyone here on the call kind of have same most questions tha- So we covered a lot of ground already. Um, but I guess, you know, just with some of the commentary around utilization, um, and with the comments you made around supply chain interruption, how much of the decline that you're seeing and yeah, I guess this comment is mostly an ITNS comment. Is related to, you kno